ne, bring the disruptor back to Gibbledon, then go right-click the second sentry stone, bring it back to Gibbledon, etc., until all eight sentry stones have been clicked._\n_If you try to enter the very center, you'll see this emote and be knocked back:_\nA barrier prevents you from entering!\n_The eight \"an active sentry stone\" are found surrounding the very center of the zone. You have to stand right under the stone for the click to take effect._\n_If you click the wrong one, you'll see:_\nYou are not near the correct sentry stone!\n_If you click the right one, you'll see:_\nThe harmonic disruptor has deactivated the sentry stone controlling the barrier to the inner section of the temple!\n_You'll then bring it back to Gibbledon for a tuning:_\nGibbledon Cogboggle quickly tunes the harmonic disruptor and then hands it back to you.\n_NOTE: After you do the first tuning with Gibbledon, golems called \"an unspeaking sentinel\" (hit for a max ~12,500) spawn all around the center area. The further you progress in the task, the more golems you'll see appearing. Killing them has no bearing on the task (although there are achievements for leaving them all alive as well as killing them all)._\n_Once you right-click a correct active sentry stone, it turns into \"a deactivated sentry stone\"._\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the first active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the second active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the third active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the fourth active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the fifth active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the sixth active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the seventh active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nUse the harmonic disruptor on the eighth active sentry stone 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nReturn the harmonic disruptor to Gibbledon so that he can tune it 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nGibbledon Cogboggle says 'All of the teleport auras that were blocking the way into the inner area of the temple should be disabled now. Unfortunately, a High Priest has appeared. Looks like you will need to take them out. Good luck!'\n_Upon the final turn-in, the center area spawns full of mobs: 1x \"High Priest Aldior\" and several \"a silentsong worshipper\" in his audience. Clear the area of mobs and then fight the High Priest._\nDefeat High Priest Aldior 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Aldior hits for a max ~18,000 and spawns adds at 75% (3x \"a musical spirit\"), 50% (3x \"a muted brute\"), and 25% (3x \"a flowing wind elemental\"):_\nHigh Priest Aldior says, in Alaran, 'Denizens of Windsong! Come to my aid!'\n_These adds are regular trash mobs (they are not weakened) and do NOT despawn upon his death._\nSpeak with Gibbledon Cogboggle 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gibbledon Cogboggle'\nGibbledon Cogboggle noisily munches on a pickle. 'Oh, you took care of that priest? Nice job. The harmonic disruptor successfully interfered with the sentry stones and allowed you access to the inner sanctum of the temple and one of the high priests, just as I knew it would! Well, my job here is done, and I suppose you are ready to [leave]. Don't forget to loot the chest for your reward before you leave!'\nLoot the treasure chest for your reward 0/1 (Windsong Sanctuary)\n_Rewards:_\n375 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip + 0-1 Valiant Ornament per task)\nBrilliant Band of Arcane Knowledge\nCoin of Weight Balancing\nDeepblade's Longshield\nEarring of Soothing Melodies\nGlowing Eyes of the Wind\nGraven Grave-Glaive\nPendant of Compelling Song\nShaded Orb of Infusion\nTendros' Healing-Stick\nWavecrasher's Raw-Hide Belt\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\nGlowing Alaran Cantrip\n- Eltarki's Diary - Music of the Mind [item=99795]",
